1
00:00:00,238 --> 00:00:10,724
你现在看到的这一切都是通过在 Claude Fable 5.1 中的一个提示词生成的，因为它在没有任何现成库的情况下运行，而且不需要二次尝试。
Everything you're watching right now came out of one prompt in Claude Fable 5.1 because it runs with no ready-made libraries and no second attempt.

2
00:00:11,054 --> 00:00:13,732
Anthropic 的新模型已经发布了。
The new model from Anthropic is already out.

3
00:00:14,030 --> 00:00:18,468
人们称它是处理你能交给它的最难任务时最强大的模型。
People are calling it the most powerful model for the hardest work you can throw at it.

4
00:00:18,734 --> 00:00:23,680
所以今天我要用真实的提示词来测试它，看看它到底表现如何。
So today I'm putting it in front of real prompts and we'll see what actually holds up.

5
00:00:23,918 --> 00:00:29,680
最后，我还会分享 7 个实用技巧，让你在发挥其最大潜力的同时降低成本。
Then at the end, I've got 7 tips for getting more out of it and paying less while you do.

6
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:40,068
Anthropic 开发这个模型是为了处理长任务，比如持续数小时的代码编写、大量的文档，以及需要经过十几个步骤才能得出结论的研究。
Anthropic built this one for the long stuff, code in sessions that run for hours, piles of documents, research that takes a dozen steps before it gets anywhere.

7
00:00:40,526 --> 00:00:46,660
有趣的是他们给出的建议，因为他们告诉你不要默认就去用它。
The unusual part is their own advice about it because they tell you not to reach for it by default.

8
00:00:47,054 --> 00:00:58,852
对于大多数普通任务，他们建议你使用 Opus 5；只有在确实需要处理复杂且多步骤的极高难度任务时，才推荐使用 Claude 3.5 Sonnet。
For most normal tasks, they point you at Opus 5 and they say Fable 5.1 for the cases where you genuinely need maximum power on something complex and multi-step.

9
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:03,524
一家公司对它最贵的模型做出这样的表态，挺让人意外的。
That's a strange thing for a company to say about its most expensive model.

10
00:01:04,110 --> 00:01:07,684
但这同时也是整篇公告中最有用的内容。
It's also the most useful line in the whole announcement.

11
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:09,764
每标记的费用没有变动。
The price per token didn't move.

12
00:01:10,094 --> 00:01:17,412
输入端是每百万标记 10 美元，输出端是 50 美元，而一个标记基本上就是一个词的一部分。
$10 per million tokens going in, 50 per million coming out, and a token is basically a chunk of a word.

13
00:01:17,742 --> 00:01:25,732
变化在于廉价的部分：当模型重新处理它已经看过的材料时，现在的成本降低了 75% ，
What changed is the cheap part when the model re-rates material it has already seen that now costs 75% less,

14
00:01:26,094 --> 00:01:28,196
降到了每百万标记 25 美分。
down to 25 cents per million.

15
00:01:28,590 --> 00:01:36,580
Anthropic 表示这能让典型任务的成本降低约四分之一，而对于繁重的多步骤工作，成本能降低近一半。
Anthropic says this pulls the cost of a typical task down by roughly a quarter, and for heavy multi-step work by almost half.

16
00:01:36,878 --> 00:01:38,756
这是他们的估算，不是我的。
That's their number, not mine.

17
00:01:39,118 --> 00:01:42,052
独立测试的结果并不总是完全一致。
Independent tests don't always land in the same place.

18
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,732
规格表上的其他内容在宏观上很大，但很难直观感受。
The rest of the spec sheet is big in a way that's hard to feel.

19
00:01:46,254 --> 00:01:55,076
它拥有大约一百万标记的上下文，通俗点说，就是你可以给它塞入海量的资料，而它才不会开始丢三落四。
It holds about a million tokens of context, which in plain language means you can throw an enormous pile of material at it before it starts losing the thread,

20
00:01:55,374 --> 00:01:59,812
而且它一次性可以写出多达 128,000 个标记的内容。
and it can write back up to 128,000 tokens in one go.

21
00:02:00,238 --> 00:02:07,120
它可以读取文本和图像，并且在回答之前会先思考，而不是直接蹦出脑子里跳出的第一反应。
It reads text and images and it thinks before it answers, instead of blurting out the first thing that comes to mind.

22
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:16,800
Anthropic 列出了它改进的 6 个方面：长篇代码编写、文档和电子表格及幻灯片、多步骤研究，
Anthropic lists 6 places where they say it improved: long coding sessions, documents and spreadsheets and slides, multi-step research,

23
00:02:16,974 --> 00:02:23,300
读取图表和示意图、可靠地利用庞大的上下文，以及自主操作界面。
reading charts and diagrams, using that huge context reliably, and driving interfaces on its own.

24
00:02:23,630 --> 00:02:24,868
这些主张可不少。
That's a lot of claims.

25
00:02:25,294 --> 00:02:27,172
测试比争论更有效。
Tests are cheaper than arguments.

26
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:32,708
开始之前还有一件事，如果你以前曾被无故拒绝过，那这很重要。
One more thing before we start, and it matters if you've ever been refused for no good reason.

27
00:02:33,166 --> 00:02:43,044
Anthropic 表示该模型现在误拦网络安全问题的比例减少了约 60%，而误拦无害的生物和医学问题的比例减少了约 85%。
Anthropic says the model now falsely blocks around 60% fewer cybersecurity questions and around 85% fewer harmless biology and medicine questions.

28
00:02:43,534 --> 00:02:45,732
实际的限制并没有消失。
The actual limits didn't disappear.

29
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:52,644
真正的渗透测试、漏洞利用编写以及严肃的生物研究，仍然会被转到其他地方处理。
Real penetration testing, exploit writing, and serious biological research still get pushed somewhere else.

30
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:55,748
所以它变得没那么敏感了，而不是变得更宽松了。
So it's less jumpy, not more permissive.

31
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:04,292
让我们看看这个模型到底有多强的智能体化能力，我选了一个复杂度高到一个人很难同时处理的任务。
Let's check how agentic this model stenkin actually is, and I picked a task with more moving parts than a person can hold in their head at once.

32
00:03:04,942 --> 00:03:12,964
两人去日本玩七天，包含机票在内的所有费用预算是3000美元，而且这两个旅行者的需求完全相反。
Seven days in Japan for two people, $3,000 for everything including the flights, and the two travelers want opposite trips.

33
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:17,700
一个想去看动漫，另一个想要森林和宁静。
One is going for anime, the other wants forests and silence.

34
00:03:18,158 --> 00:03:27,844
除此之外，它还得找出10月份真实的航班选项，筛选出三家酒店，并制定出一份能让两人都满意的逐小时行程单。
On top of that, it has to pull real flight options for October, shortlist three hotels, and lay out an hour by hour route that keeps both of them happy.

35
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:35,364
我在发送之前开启了思考模式，这样你可以看到它是如何解决问题的，而不只是看最终的计划。
I turn thinking mode on before I send it, so you can watch it work the problem instead of just reading the finished plan.

36
00:03:35,694 --> 00:03:40,676
就在这里，普通的聊天机器人和更接近智能体的模型拉开了差距。
This is the line where a chatbot and something closer to an agent separate.

37
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:46,852
聊天机器人只会给你一份看起来很漂亮、带有一堆看似合理的数字的行程单。
A chatbot hands you a beautiful itinerary with plausible sounding numbers attached.

38
00:03:47,278 --> 00:03:57,572
我想看到的是计算是否准确，比如在预留酒店费用后，3000美元还能覆盖两张机票吗，以及它是否会注明价格是估算的
What I want to see is the arithmetic holding up, whether $3,000 still covers two flights after it takes those hotels, and whether it says a price is an estimate

39
00:03:57,838 --> 00:04:00,260
而不是编造一个根本不存在的预订。
instead of inventing a booking that doesn't exist.

40
00:04:01,006 --> 00:04:02,532
接下来是人类层面的考量。
Then there's the human part.

41
00:04:02,894 --> 00:04:08,644
差劲的回答只是简单地交替安排一天动漫、一天宁静，就管这叫平衡。
The weak answer alternates one anime day with one quiet day and calls that balance.

42
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:15,232
好的回答会先理清地理位置，确保没人为了所谓的礼貌而在火车上浪费四个小时。
A good one fixes the geography first, so nobody burns four hours on a train being polite.

43
00:04:15,406 --> 00:04:16,548
这是它给出的结果。
And here's what came back.

44
00:04:16,974 --> 00:04:17,860
预算是合理的。
The budget holds.

45
00:04:18,350 --> 00:04:28,932
机票、三家酒店、餐饮和当地火车都在3000以内，而且它把机票价格标注为估算，而不是假装已经订好了。
Flights, three hotels, food, and local trains all fit under 3000, and it marks the flight prices as estimates instead of pretending it booked something.

46
00:04:29,486 --> 00:04:30,660
这是很诚实的做法。
That's the honest move.

47
00:04:31,022 --> 00:04:33,312
路线也是按地理位置分组的。
The route is grouped by geography as well.

48
00:04:33,614 --> 00:04:36,868
动漫相关的行程集中在开头的东京阶段。
The anime days sit together at the start in Tokyo.

49
00:04:37,166 --> 00:04:43,940
然后两人一起去山里度过宁静的一半旅程，这样就不会有人为了所谓的礼貌而在火车上浪费4小时。
Then both of them head out to the mountains for the quiet half, so nobody burns 4 hours on a train being polite.

50
00:04:44,334 --> 00:04:50,532
虽然在几个地方关于穿越这么大城市的速度，它的逐小时时间安排有点过于乐观。
The hour by hour timing is optimistic in a couple of places about how fast you cross a city that size.

51
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:53,252
但它底层的思考逻辑是正确的。
But the thinking underneath it is right.

52
00:04:53,838 --> 00:05:00,036
它先解决了约束条件，然后再写计划，这正是我希望从这个模型中得到的表现。
It solved the constraints first and wrote the plan second, and that's exactly the behavior I wanted out of this one.

53
00:05:00,462 --> 00:05:04,912
那个旅行提示词正是我不信任单一模型的理由。
That trip prompt is exactly why I never trust one model on its own.

54
00:05:05,134 --> 00:05:08,592
只有当另一个答案放在它旁边时，你才能看出一个回答到底有多好。
You only see how good an answer is when another one sits next to it.

55
00:05:08,782 --> 00:05:14,660
为了这个去订阅四个账号成本太高，所以我用自己的平台，AI Master。
Running four subscriptions for that is expensive, so I do it in my own platform, AI Master.

56
00:05:14,992 --> 00:05:21,380
一个窗口，一个登录，Claude、Chat GBT、Grok 和 Gemini 并排显示。
One window, one login, Claude, Chat GBT, Grok and Gemini side by side.

57
00:05:21,614 --> 00:05:24,832
而且每标记的费用比分别支付给每一个模型都要便宜。
And cheaper per token than paying for each of them separately.

58
00:05:25,166 --> 00:05:26,884
聊天只是其中的一部分。
The chat is one piece of it.

59
00:05:27,152 --> 00:05:30,832
图片、语音和视频都在同一个地方生成。
Images, voice, and video generate in the same place.

60
00:05:31,072 --> 00:05:37,152
而且更便宜，而且你可以让一个角色在每一次生成中看起来都一模一样。
Also cheaper, and you can keep one character who looks identical across every generation.

61
00:05:37,326 --> 00:05:41,188
那个角色可以发布并直接为你赚钱。
That character can be published and earn money for you right there.

62
00:05:41,582 --> 00:05:45,872
你创作的任何内容都会分享到动态中，帮你增加曝光量。
Whatever you make gets shared into the feed so it works for your reach.

63
00:05:46,318 --> 00:05:55,472
Bearable 能与你的团队和 AI 智能体一起运营整个频道，负责写脚本、写描述、剪辑视频和图片，并制作缩略图。
Bearable runs a full channel with your team and AI agents writing scripts and descriptions, editing video and images, and building thumbnails.

64
00:05:55,662 --> 00:06:07,472
学院包含 200 多节课程，大约 30 小时。在网站上你可以看到真实的结果和案例，还有用户分享效果的截图和演示视频。
The Academy holds over 200 lessons, roughly 30 hours. On the site you'll see real results and cases, screenshots and demo videos of people saying what it did for them.

65
00:06:07,712 --> 00:06:11,108
社区里已经有超过 1.5 万人了。
More than 15,000 people are in the community already.

66
00:06:11,438 --> 00:06:13,892
路径很短，我会在屏幕上点出来。
The path is short, and I'll click it on screen.

67
00:06:14,126 --> 00:06:17,764
去 amaster.me 并选择年度订阅。
You go to amaster.me and take the annual subscription.

68
00:06:18,222 --> 00:06:21,872
就是我建议你选的那一个，因为那里有折扣。
That's the one I tell you to get since the discount sits there.

69
00:06:22,094 --> 00:06:23,780
然后你就进入账户了。
Then you're inside the account.

70
00:06:24,206 --> 00:06:27,012
如果觉得不合适，可以在七天内退款。
Seven days to take your money back if it isn't for you.

71
00:06:27,342 --> 00:06:28,388
这就是我的工具组合。
That's my stack.

72
00:06:28,718 --> 00:06:30,884
现在回到 Claude 3.5 Sonnet。
Now back to Fable 5.1.

73
00:06:31,072 --> 00:06:34,192
让我们来看看 Claude 3.5 Sonnet 的视觉处理能力。
Let's check the visual side of Fable 5.1.

74
00:06:34,432 --> 00:06:40,352
读懂清晰的截图是一回事，但辨认我自己的手写体完全是另一项挑战。
Reading a clean screenshot is one thing, but reading my own handwriting is a different test entirely.

75
00:06:40,592 --> 00:06:43,684
我在一张纸上草绘了一个基础的应用流程。
I sketch a basic app flow on a sheet of paper.

76
00:06:44,078 --> 00:06:47,172
登录、首页、产品、卡片、结账。
Login, home, product, card, checkout.

77
00:06:47,534 --> 00:06:49,476
我故意画得很乱。
I draw it messy, on purpose.

78
00:06:50,222 --> 00:06:53,508
方框没对齐，箭头互相交叉。
The boxes don't line up and arrows cross each other.

79
00:06:53,774 --> 00:06:57,508
因为空间不够，一个屏幕被挤到了角落。
One screen ends up crammed into the corner because I ran out of room.

80
00:06:57,902 --> 00:07:02,308
我用手机拍下这张纸，直接扔进对话框。
I photograph the paper with my phone and drop it straight into the chat.

81
00:07:02,798 --> 00:07:04,260
要求有三点。
The ask is three things.

82
00:07:04,846 --> 00:07:11,780
把这些涂鸦变成清晰的流程图，找出过程中任何逻辑断层的地方，并告诉我漏掉了哪些步骤。
Turn the scribble into a clean flow, catch anything that breaks along the way, and tell me what step is missing.

83
00:07:11,952 --> 00:07:14,244
识别内容只是第一步。
Reading it is only the first job.

84
00:07:14,606 --> 00:07:22,628
现在的模型都能转录粗糙的手写体了，而且大多数模型到此为止，只会把你的草图整理成整洁的副本。
Any model can transcribe rough handwriting by now, and most stop right there, handing back a tidy copy of your own drawing.

85
00:07:23,086 --> 00:07:24,912
我要的是更高一层的处理。
I want the layer above that.

86
00:07:25,198 --> 00:07:29,472
当线条重叠时，它必须判断出哪个箭头连接到哪个方框。
It has to work out which arrow connects to which box when the lines overlap.

87
00:07:29,966 --> 00:07:35,972
然后它还要指出流程中任何不符合应用逻辑的地方。
Then it has to flag anything about the flow itself that doesn't actually make sense as an app.

88
00:07:36,334 --> 00:07:43,940
这是模型通常会回避的部分，因为指出别人逻辑中的漏洞比单纯复制内容要冒险得多。
That's the part models usually dodge, because pointing at a hole in someone's logic is riskier than just copying it.

89
00:07:44,112 --> 00:07:45,872
而它正确读出了所有内容。
And it reads all of it correctly.

90
00:07:46,032 --> 00:07:52,036
纸上的每个方框都准确对位，甚至在两个箭头交叉的地方也处理得很好。
Every box from the paper lands in the right place, with the arrows sorted out even where two of them cross.

91
00:07:52,494 --> 00:07:54,916
它还能发现流程中的真实漏洞。
It also catches real gaps in the flow.

92
00:07:55,278 --> 00:08:01,636
用户点击支付后，没地方跳转，没有订单确认，也没有明确的下一步操作。
After the user hits pay, there's nowhere to go, no order confirmation, and no clear next step.

93
00:08:02,222 --> 00:08:04,868
结账页面也没法退回到卡片界面。
Checkout has no way back to the card either.

94
00:08:05,198 --> 00:08:09,476
它把这些标记为流程中的问题，而不是我绘图时的错误。
It flags those as problems in the flow, not mistakes in my drawing.

95
00:08:09,870 --> 00:08:18,276
然后它构建了一个改进的第二个版本，并添加了我完全没画出的步骤，包括支付失败状态和订单确认。
Then it builds a second, improved version, and adds the steps I hadn't drawn at all, including a failed payment state and an order confirmation.

96
00:08:18,766 --> 00:08:20,160
这才是有用的部分。
That's the useful part.

97
00:08:20,558 --> 00:08:22,800
理清这些乱七八糟的内容只是入门门槛。
Reading the mess was just the entry fee.

98
00:08:23,022 --> 00:08:29,732
如果你正在经营业务，现在还要同时操作 10 种不同的工具，如果我告诉你有一个平台就能取代所有这些工具呢？
If you're running a business and juggling 10 different tools right now, what if I told you that one platform could replace all of them?

99
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:31,200
这就是 Go High Level。
This is Go High Level.

100
00:08:31,374 --> 00:08:33,760
你可以使用几乎所有的功能。
You get access to pretty much all the features.

101
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,280
社交媒体规划器。
Social media planner.

102
00:08:35,693 --> 00:08:41,919
你可以安排发布内容，查看你的内容日历，甚至可以一键在多个平台上转发内容。
You can schedule posts, see your content calendar, and even repost content across multiple platforms with one click.

103
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:42,880
邮件营销。
Email marketing.

104
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:45,440
Go High Level 有一套完整的邮件工具。
Go high level has a full email suite.

105
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:49,920
你可以创建活动，并使用拖拽编辑器制作邮件模板。
You can create campaigns, build email templates with a drag and drop editor.

106
00:08:50,126 --> 00:08:53,360
Go High Level 内置了日历和预约系统。
Go high level has a built-in calendar and booking system.

107
00:08:53,454 --> 00:08:55,360
这可以替代像 Calendly 之类的工具。
This replaces tools like Calendly.

108
00:08:55,630 --> 00:09:02,560
你可以创建不同类型的日历，包括一对一会议、群组通话，如果你有团队，还可以设置轮流预约。
You can create different calendar types, one-on-one meetings, group calls, round robin scheduling if you have a team.

109
00:09:02,766 --> 00:09:03,760
最棒的部分来了。
And here's the best part.

110
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,520
Go High Level 有大量的预设工作流模板。
Go high level has a ton of pre-built workflow templates.

111
00:09:07,694 --> 00:09:14,800
我在描述栏里放了一个 30 天的免费试用链接，不是标准的 14 天，而是专属的延长试用。
I've linked a 30-day free trial in the description, not the standard 14 days, an exclusive extended trial.

112
00:09:15,054 --> 00:09:22,276
Claude 3.5 Sonnet 现在可以进行端到端的 3D 建模，而且它是通过代码而非建模软件来完成的。
Fable 5.1 can now do end-to-end 3D modeling, and it does that through code instead of a modeling program.

113
00:09:22,670 --> 00:09:28,004
所以让我们测试一个模型除了布局之外几乎没有任何参考信息的任务。
So let's test it on something where the model has almost nothing to work with except the layout.

114
00:09:28,590 --> 00:09:35,876
我没有用文字描述最终场景，而是给它一张中世纪城堡房间的 2D 俯视图。
Instead of describing the finished scene in words, I give it a 2D top-down floor plan of a medieval castle room.

115
00:09:36,590 --> 00:09:44,880
其中一面墙上有壁炉，两侧有窗户，中间有一张长餐桌，还有柱子、一个高台，
There's a fireplace on one wall, windows on both sides, a long dining table in the middle, columns, a raised platform,

116
00:09:45,070 --> 00:09:50,340
以及一把宝座，所有这些都作为从正上方看到的简单形状和标签绘制出来。
and a throne, all drawn as simple shapes and labels seen straight from above.

117
00:09:50,734 --> 00:09:55,172
没有成品房间的图片，没有透视效果，只有一个平面图。
No image of the finished room, no perspective, just a flat plan.

118
00:09:55,822 --> 00:10:00,996
然后我要求它根据这个完全相同的布局，制作出三个完整的 3D 版本。
Then I ask for three fully built 3D versions of that exact same layout.

119
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,556
哥特式、废弃风格和皇家风格。
Gothic, abandoned, and royal.

120
00:10:03,982 --> 00:10:07,492
这三个版本都必须在构件中以交互式形式运行。
All three have to run interactively inside an artifact.

121
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:10,000
三个变体，只有一个平面图。
Three variants, one flat drawing.

122
00:10:10,254 --> 00:10:12,132
这个要求里隐藏了很多细节。
There's a lot hiding in that request.

123
00:10:12,526 --> 00:10:18,116
平面图决定了物品的位置，但几乎没提到它们在三维空间中长什么样。
The floor plan tells it where things go, but almost nothing about what they look like in three dimensions.

124
00:10:18,606 --> 00:10:29,508
模型必须决定墙有多高、窗户有多深、柱子多高，以及壁炉和高台如何融入房间。
The model has to decide how high the walls are, how deep the windows sit, how tall the columns should be, and how the fireplace and raised platform actually fit into the room.

125
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:36,388
甚至家具也得按正确的比例放置，而不是看起来像个娃娃屋或者悬浮在地面上。
Even the furniture has to land at the right scale, instead of looking like a dollhouse or floating above the floor.

126
00:10:36,846 --> 00:10:46,916
然后它得把这些全部做三遍，在保持平面图不变的同时，改变材质、状态和灯光，让房间感觉完全不同，
And then it has to do all of that three times, holding the same floor plan steady while changing the materials, condition, and lighting enough that the rooms actually feel different,

127
00:10:47,182 --> 00:10:49,412
而不是同一个城堡只是套了不同的滤镜。
not the same castle under a different filter.

128
00:10:49,614 --> 00:10:50,852
这就是它构建出来的结果。
And here's what it built.

129
00:10:51,214 --> 00:10:53,220
三个版本都遵循了平面图。
All three versions follow the plan.

130
00:10:53,646 --> 00:11:06,276
壁炉、窗户、桌子、柱子、王座和高台都在我画的位置，而且房间的比例看起来很真实，而不是感觉是围绕镜头生成的。
The fireplace, windows, table, columns, throne, and raised platform stay where I drew them, and the room reads at a believable scale instead of feeling generated around the camera.

131
00:11:07,086 --> 00:11:12,932
哥特式版本使用了陈旧的石头、老木材和温暖的火光，显得阴暗厚重。
The gothic version is dark and heavy with aged stone, old wood, and warm firelight.

132
00:11:13,230 --> 00:11:22,628
废弃版保留了同样的房间，但让它破败不堪，表面有裂缝，家具受损，布满灰尘，窗户透进来的光线也更冷一些。
The abandoned version keeps the same room but lets it fall apart, with cracked surfaces, damaged furniture, dust, and colder light coming through the windows.

133
00:11:23,118 --> 00:11:29,380
皇家版本用更整洁的石头、抛光的木材、挂毯和更温暖的灯光进行了修复。
The Royal version restores it with cleaner stone, polished wood, tapestries, and warmer lighting.

134
00:11:29,774 --> 00:11:33,028
在它们之间切换，能让核心重点变得很明显。
And switching between them makes the important part obvious.

135
00:11:33,262 --> 00:11:34,756
几何结构没有变动。
The geometry doesn't move.

136
00:11:35,086 --> 00:11:38,020
这三个版本底层的空间都是一样的。
It's still the same room underneath all three.

137
00:11:38,414 --> 00:11:46,820
这就是我之前担心的部分：模型是否能理解风格的词汇，但在应用时又不破坏原始计划。
That's the part I was worried about walking in, a model that understands the vocabulary of a style, but loses the actual plan while applying it.

138
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:49,028
这个模型同时兼顾了这两点。
This one kept both.

139
00:11:49,486 --> 00:11:52,708
测试 4 测试的是纯代码编写，不允许使用任何辅助工具。
Test 4 checks pure coding with no crutches allowed.

140
00:11:53,038 --> 00:11:57,828
我对模型提出了严格限制，并且禁止使用任何外部图形库。
I put a hard constraint on the model and then every outside graphics library.

141
00:11:58,062 --> 00:12:05,892
任务是仅用原生 JavaScript 从头开始构建一个诺顿光影模拟器，并在聊天中的构件里交互运行。
The task is to build a Norton Light simulator from scratch in plain JavaScript, running interactively inside an artifact in the chat.

142
00:12:06,318 --> 00:12:11,172
包含三个可操作的滑块：运动速度、颜色亮度和星体密度。
At three working sliders, movement speed, color brightness, and star density.

143
00:12:11,502 --> 00:12:13,680
一个提示词，一次尝试，没有任何帮助。
One prompt, one attempt, no help.

144
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:16,068
最后那行字就是整个测试的核心。
That last line is the whole test.

145
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:19,332
没有库支持，意味着没有任何现成的东西提供给它。
With no library, nothing is handed to it.

146
00:12:19,790 --> 00:12:28,868
模型必须自己推敲出光幕如何弯曲和漂移，以及颜色如何融入黑暗，而不是在硬边界处戛然而止。
The model has to work out how a curtain of light bends and drifts, and how the color fades into the dark instead of stopping on a hard line.

147
00:12:29,614 --> 00:12:35,492
星星是另一个难题，如果分布不好，看起来就像个网格而不是天空。
Stars are their own problem because scattered badly they read as a grid instead of a sky.

148
00:12:35,982 --> 00:12:38,692
真实的极光是缓慢且不均匀的。
Real Aurora is slow and uneven.

149
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:44,800
它在某些地方变亮，而在其他地方变暗，而且它不像屏幕保护程序那样循环播放。
It brightens in one place while it fades in another, and it never loops like a screensaver.

150
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:49,988
接下来是那些滑块，听起来像是小细节，但其实不然。
Then there are the sliders, which sound like a small detail and aren't.

151
00:12:50,734 --> 00:12:54,116
速度应该只改变运动，而不去动颜色。
Speed should change the motion and leave the color alone.

152
00:12:54,574 --> 00:12:58,244
强度必须改变亮度，而不能让漂移卡住。
Intensity has to change brightness without freezing the drift.

153
00:12:58,734 --> 00:13:03,908
当一个模型只能理解一半代码时，这些滑块就是体现出来的地方。
When a model only half understands its own code, the sliders are where that shows.

154
00:13:04,174 --> 00:13:05,476
这是它画出来的东西。
And here's what it drew.

155
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:08,708
天空的移动方式和真实情况一致。
The sky moves the way the real thing moves.

156
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:16,644
窗帘漂移不均匀，一部分变亮而另一部分变暗，边缘也融入黑暗而非在一条线上截止。
The curtains drift unevenly, one part brightens while another fades, and the edges bleed into the dark instead of ending on a line.

157
00:13:17,006 --> 00:13:21,120
星星散布在其中，没有透出的网格。这个
The stars sit scattered with no grid showing through them. The

158
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:24,228
滑块是我预期会出问题的地方，但它们没坏。
sliders are the part I expected to break, and they don't.

159
00:13:24,558 --> 00:13:33,380
我在场景动画播放时把三个参数都推到极端，因为中间位置总是看起来没问题，而且每个参数只影响它该影响的部分。
I push all three to both extremes while the scene is animating, because the middle always looks fine, and each one only touches what it's supposed to.

160
00:13:33,902 --> 00:13:36,932
速度改变漂移，而不去动颜色。
Speed changes the drift and leaves the color alone.

161
00:13:37,390 --> 00:13:40,560
星辰密度是增加星星，而不是重绘天空。
Star density adds stars instead of repainting the sky.

162
00:13:40,814 --> 00:13:45,220
在最高密度时确实会卡顿，这是整个系统唯一出问题的地方。
At maximum density it does stutter, and that's the one place the whole thing slips.

163
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:51,440
这是仅用一次尝试从零开始生成的，是所有测试中最接近实际工作的。
Written from nothing in a single attempt, this is the closest any of these tests gets to real work.

164
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:58,980
测试 5 是一个完整的第一人称射击游戏，它必须通过单个提示词出现在构件的窗口里。
Test 5 is a full first-person shooter, and it has to appear inside the artifact's window from a single prompt.

165
00:13:59,374 --> 00:14:01,572
主题是外星人入侵。
The theme is an alien invasion.

166
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:07,780
玩家站在空间站的霓虹竞技场中，手里拿着爆破枪，屏幕上有准心。
The player stands in a neon arena on a space station with a blaster and a crosshair on screen.

167
00:14:08,174 --> 00:14:11,652
你用 WSD 移动，用鼠标环顾四周。
You walk with WSD and look around with the mouse.

168
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:14,084
左键发射激光。
Left click fires the laser.

169
00:14:14,350 --> 00:14:24,260
敌人是飞碟和触手生物，由带有霓虹绿或紫色光芒的球体和圆柱体构成，它们在竞技场里追捕你。
The enemies are flying saucers and tentacle creatures built out of spheres and cylinders with a neon green or violet glow, and they hunt you across the arena.

170
00:14:24,718 --> 00:14:31,588
除此之外，我还要难度递增的波次、一个血条、爆破枪上的过热量表，还有一个击杀计数器。
On top of that, I want waves that get harder, a health bar, an overheat gauge on the blaster, and a counter for kills.

171
00:14:31,950 --> 00:14:34,560
一个提示词，一次尝试，而且它必须能运行。
One prompt, one attempt, and it has to run.

172
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,580
这些几乎都不是绘图任务。
Almost none of that is drawing.

173
00:14:36,942 --> 00:14:43,012
鼠标视角必须抓取光标并保持平滑，否则在头两秒内就会感觉像坏了一样。
The mouse look has to grab the cursor and stay smooth, or the thing feels broken in the first two seconds.

174
00:14:43,374 --> 00:14:52,772
外星人没有模型需要下载，它们的身体由一些基础几何体组成，但这些几何体仍要看起来像生物而不是一堆球。
The aliens have no model to download, so their bodies come out of a handful of primitives that still have to read as a creature instead of a pile of balls.

175
00:14:53,230 --> 00:15:00,196
然后它们必须进行追猎，这意味着每一艘飞碟都要在每一帧追踪玩家，且不会穿墙。
Then they have to hunt, which means every saucer tracks the player each frame without sliding through a wall.

176
00:15:00,558 --> 00:15:09,060
过热量表是那个隐蔽的环节。只有当按住扳机太久真的切断激光并让你等待时，它才有意义。
The overheat gauge is the sneaky one. It only means anything if holding the trigger too long actually cuts the laser and makes you wait.

177
00:15:09,390 --> 00:15:13,760
而且波次必须不断升级，而不是让第二轮变成一道无法逾越的墙。
And the waves have to climb without turning round 2 into a brick wall.

178
00:15:13,998 --> 00:15:15,044
这是它构建出来的东西。
And here's what it built.

179
00:15:15,438 --> 00:15:21,540
竞技场渲染出来了，鼠标视角很稳，飞碟按波次出现，且每轮变得更密集。
The arena renders, the mouse look holds steady, and the saucers come in waves that get thicker every round.

180
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:24,068
当你击败它们时，击杀计数器就会上升。
The kill counter climbs as you drop them.

181
00:15:24,718 --> 00:15:33,124
当你按住扳机时，过热条会填满并关闭激光直到冷却，而我原本预期它会完全跳过这个机制。
The overheat bar fills while you hold the trigger and shuts the laser down until it cools, which is the mechanic I expected it to skip entirely.

182
00:15:33,550 --> 00:15:35,780
当有东西靠近你时，生命值会下降。
Health drops when something reaches you.

183
00:15:36,046 --> 00:15:38,116
那些粗糙的部分就是你预料中的那些。
The rough parts are the ones you'd guess.

184
00:15:38,798 --> 00:15:46,916
外星人的身体被识别为带触手的球体，而且敌人之间几乎不会发生碰撞，所以它们会堆叠在同一个位置。
Alien bodies read as spheres with tentacles glued on, and the enemies barely collide with each other, so they stack into the same spot.

185
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:09,060
在普通的聊天窗口中，不需要任何设置。
In the normal chat window, no setup involved.

186
00:16:09,646 --> 00:16:14,948
最后三条是给那些深度使用 Claude Code 的人的，等我们讲到那里时我会说明的。
The last three are for people who live inside Claude Code, and I'll say so when we get there.

187
00:16:15,566 --> 00:16:18,820
从较低的努力程度开始，而不是调高。
Start with the effort level and turn it down instead of up.

188
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:24,160
这是大家在第一天就会搞错的设置，因为「最大」听起来似乎更好。
This is the setting people get wrong on day one, because maximum sounds like better.

189
00:16:24,494 --> 00:16:33,280
Code Rabbit 对两种模式都进行了同样的评估，低努力度发现的问题比高努力度多，分别是 61% 对比 57%。
Code Rabbit ran the same review both ways, and low effort caught more problems than high effort did, 61% against 57.

190
00:16:33,774 --> 00:16:36,388
而且它还快了近 3 分钟。
It also finished almost 3 minutes faster.

191
00:16:36,718 --> 00:16:42,340
我自己的测试结果也是一样的，每次对比时，低努力度模式都更好且更快。
My own runs came out the same way, better and quicker on low every time I lined them up.

192
00:16:42,734 --> 00:16:49,252
所以先设低点，只有当输出结果确实有理由去提高时才调高，但大多数时候都不需要。
So start low, raise it only when the output gives you an actual reason to, and most of the time it won't.

193
00:16:49,710 --> 00:16:54,640
下一条能让你避免在处理长任务时产生的习惯性问题。
The next one saves you from a habit that shows up on every long job.

194
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:56,800
告诉它没有人在旁边看着。
Tell it that nobody is watching.

195
00:16:57,006 --> 00:17:05,358
默认情况下，它表现得好像有人坐在它旁边一样，所以在执行长任务到一半时，它会停下来请求许可去执行下一步。
Out of the box, it behaves like there's a person sitting next to it, so halfway through a long job, it stops and asks permission for a step

196
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,780
而你的原始请求已经涵盖了这一步。
your original request already covered.

197
00:17:08,079 --> 00:17:10,468
直接把修复方案写进提示词里。
Write the fix straight into the prompt.

198
00:17:10,925 --> 00:17:17,796
说明这里没人，并且只要操作可以撤销，它就应该继续完成请求涵盖的所有内容。
Say there's no one here, and that it should keep going through everything the request covers as long as the action can be undone.

199
00:17:18,252 --> 00:17:21,188
这样它就不会再问那些根本没必要问的问题了。
It stops asking questions it never needed to ask.

200
00:17:21,868 --> 00:17:29,956
这并不能解决超长会话中的偏移问题，而且它仍然可能写出运行正常但却在悄悄做错事的代码。
That doesn't cure the drift on very long sessions, and it still writes code that runs fine while quietly doing the wrong thing.

201
00:17:30,350 --> 00:17:32,496
无论如何，你最后还是得去检查输出结果。
You read the output at the end regardless.

202
00:17:32,782 --> 00:17:36,336
下一条在处理庞大且复杂的任务时最为重要。
This next one matters most when the job is big and ugly.

203
00:17:36,622 --> 00:17:38,308
一次性把整件事都交给它。
Give it the whole thing at once.

204
00:17:38,670 --> 00:17:41,860
看看 Anthropic 选择用这个模型展示什么。
Look at what Anthropic chose to show off with this model.

205
00:17:42,126 --> 00:17:51,460
这不是一个编程演示，他们用几十年前的麦哲伦号探测金星的雷达数据来运行它，并让它全程完成分析工作。
It wasn't a coding demo, they ran it across decades-old radar data from the Magellan mission to Venus and let it work the analysis all the way through.

206
00:17:51,790 --> 00:17:53,668
这告诉你它的强项在哪里。
That tells you where it earns its money.

207
00:17:54,062 --> 00:18:02,340
在我自己的测试中最难的任务中，它的完成速度比 Claude 3 Opus 快了约 40%，而且成本也显著降低。
On the hardest task in my own testing, it finished about 40% faster than Fable 5, and cost meaningfully less getting there.

208
00:18:02,766 --> 00:18:05,124
在简单的任务上，旧模型表现更好。
On simple work, the old model did better.

209
00:18:05,454 --> 00:18:08,228
所以不要把一个功能拆成 8 个小提示词。
So don't chop a feature into 8 little prompts.

210
00:18:08,718 --> 00:18:13,056
描述你想要的最终结果，让它自己跑到最后。
Describe the finished result you want and let it run to the end on its own.

211
00:18:13,296 --> 00:18:16,196
最后一个在任何地方都管用的技巧是关于它如何写作的。
The last one that works anywhere is about how it writes.

212
00:18:16,814 --> 00:18:18,916
要求它去掉堆砌辞藻的文体。
Ask it to drop the mannered prose.

213
00:18:19,246 --> 00:18:27,776
Claude 3.5 Sonnet 使用华丽比喻的频率低于 Opus 5 和之前的 Claude 3 Opus，所以关于“杠杆”之类的废话会少一些
Fable 5.1 reaches for fancy metaphors less than Opus 5 and the old Fable 5 did, so you get fewer lines about levers

214
00:18:27,936 --> 00:18:31,108
当诚实的表述被改为设置时，这些内容就没必要了。
worth pulling when the honest version is changed to setting.

215
00:18:31,662 --> 00:18:33,124
不过这种习惯还没消失。
The habit isn't gone though.

216
00:18:33,646 --> 00:18:41,188
现在的句子变长了，段落间的停顿变少，导致长回答变得比实际需要的更难阅读。
Sentences also come out longer now, with fewer breaks between paragraphs, which makes a long answer harder to read than it needs to be.

217
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:44,356
在提示词里加一行就能同时解决这两个问题。
One line in your prompt fixes both at once.

218
00:18:44,718 --> 00:18:46,640
要求它去掉所有堆砌辞藻的文体。
Ask it to drop all mannered prose.

219
00:18:47,056 --> 00:18:50,724
这就是我用的准确措辞，这样写出来的文字就会变得平实。
That's the exact phrase I use, and the writing comes back plain.

220
00:18:50,990 --> 00:18:56,356
现在用同样的逻辑，但专门针对抓取到的代码，并从清理工作开始。
Now the same logic, but for clawed code specifically, and it starts with a cleanup job.

221
00:18:56,686 --> 00:18:59,428
删掉你为旧模型写的指令。
Delete the instructions you wrote for the old model.

222
00:18:59,696 --> 00:19:08,772
你为了修正 Claude 3 Opus 的行为而添加的每一个规则，在你的 Claude.md 里可能都是过时的内容。
Every rule you added to patch the behavior of Fable 5, where something older than that is still sitting in your Claude.md right now.

223
00:19:09,134 --> 00:19:14,564
新模型会阅读全部内容，并浪费精力去修复那些它已经不再存在的问题。
The new model reads all of it and burns effort fixing problems it doesn't have anymore.

224
00:19:14,926 --> 00:19:16,388
测试这一点很简单。
Testing that is easy.

225
00:19:16,686 --> 00:19:22,596
拿掉一条指令，运行同样的任务，如果没有任何变化，那行就是多余的负担。
Pull one instruction out, run the same task, and if nothing changes, that line was dead weight.

226
00:19:23,022 --> 00:19:31,204
还有一个终端命令叫 Claude API 提示词 audit，它会寻找过时的内容并建议具体的修改。
There is also a terminal command, Claude API prompt audit, that goes looking for the stale ones and suggests specific edits.

227
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:35,216
它只会给出建议，绝不会擅自修改你的文件。
It only suggests it never touches your files by itself.

228
00:19:35,470 --> 00:19:38,692
下一个技巧源于它过度热心的行为。
The next one comes out of the same overhelpfulness.

229
00:19:39,056 --> 00:19:41,508
明确规定哪些内容它不准动。
Name what it isn't allowed to touch.

230
00:19:41,870 --> 00:19:44,900
这个模型有个习惯，就是喜欢做一些你没要求的事。
This model has a habit of doing more than you asked.

231
00:19:45,358 --> 00:19:51,300
你请求一个功能，它在处理时会顺便决定把旁边的东西也整理一下。
You request one feature and while it's in there, it decides to tidy up something next door.

232
00:19:52,014 --> 00:19:58,436
我有次要求一个功能，它居然把我的测试文件给重写了，而这根本没人提过。
I asked for a feature once and it went and rewrote my test files, which nobody had mentioned at any point.

233
00:19:58,862 --> 00:20:04,292
所以就在提示词里列出那些不准动的内容，再加一行。
So list the things that stay untouched right there in the prompt and add one more line.

234
00:20:04,654 --> 00:20:10,660
如果它发现其他问题，它会在最后提到这些问题，而不是擅自去修复它们。
If it notices another problem, it mentions that at the end instead of fixing it on its own initiative.

235
00:20:11,150 --> 00:20:14,564
这样你既能得到想要的修复，还能看到关于其他部分的说明。
You get the fix you asked for and a note about the rest.

236
00:20:14,894 --> 00:20:17,700
最后一个直接体现在你的账单上。
And the last one shows up straight on your bill.

237
00:20:18,030 --> 00:20:20,772
让它只修改文件，而不是重写整个文件。
Make it edit the file instead of rewriting it.

238
00:20:21,166 --> 00:20:26,564
如果不加限制，当实际变动只有四行时，它会重新生成整个文件。
Left alone, it will regenerate an entire file when the actual change is four lines.

239
00:20:27,054 --> 00:20:31,236
结果是一样的，但你得为输出的每一个标记支付费用。
Same result, and you pay for every one of those output tokens on the way out.

240
00:20:31,726 --> 00:20:36,740
所以只要能达到同样效果，就告诉它只修改需要修改的部分。
So tell it to edit only the part that needs editing whenever that gets you the same thing.

241
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:39,940
对于一个很小的脚本，没人会注意到区别。
On one small script, nobody notices the difference.

242
00:20:40,270 --> 00:20:46,180
但在包含几百个文件的项目中，这就会变成真金白银的支出，而你只需要在提示词里加一句话就能解决。
On a project with a few hundred files, it turns into real money, and it's one sentence in your prompt.

243
00:20:46,496 --> 00:20:49,828
在你设置这一切的过程中，还有两个能省钱的小技巧。
Two smaller money things while you're setting all this up.

244
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:59,204
更便宜的重复读取只在同一个对话中生效，所以如果你上传一个大文档，然后针对每一个后续问题都开个新对话，
The cheaper rereading only counts inside the same conversation, so if you drop a big document in and then open a fresh chat for every follow-up

245
00:20:59,376 --> 00:21:04,816
你每次都要付全价，你的账单就跟官方公告完全对不上。
question, you pay full price each time, and your bill looks nothing like the announcement.

246
00:21:05,070 --> 00:21:15,044
相反，保留一个长对话，把那个一百万标记的窗口当成上限而不是承诺，因为一段素材离你的问题越远，
Keep one long thread instead, and treat that million token window as a ceiling rather than a promise, because the further a piece of material sits from your question,

247
00:21:15,216 --> 00:21:16,868
它就越有可能被略过。
the more likely it gets skimmed.

248
00:21:17,296 --> 00:21:21,616
把重要的内容直接放在问题旁边，那数量就不太重要了。
Put what matters right next to the question, and the number stops mattering much.

249
00:21:21,902 --> 00:21:25,136
关于你刚看到的这些测试，最后说点实话。
One last piece of honesty about the tests you just watched.

250
00:21:25,616 --> 00:21:35,172
每一个测试都是单次提示词和单次尝试，因为这是在没有任何保障的情况下，公平衡量它实际能力的最公平方式。
Every one of them was a single prompt and a single attempt, because that's the only fair way to see what it can actually do without a safety net.

251
00:21:35,376 --> 00:21:37,764
实际上没人会那样工作。
Nobody actually works like that.

252
00:21:38,126 --> 00:21:45,316
在实际使用中，你会去纠正它，重跑出错的部分，并引导它走向你想要的结果，这正是它的强项所在。
In real use, you correct it, Rerun the broken part and push it toward what you meant, and that's where it's strongest.

253
00:21:45,774 --> 00:21:47,556
这是我经过五个测试后的结论。
My verdict after five tests.

254
00:21:48,046 --> 00:21:53,860
Claude 3.5 Sonnet 是个巨大的飞跃，而打动我的并不是那些花里胡哨的测试。
Fable 5.1 is a real step up, and the tests that moved me weren't the flashy ones.

255
00:21:54,096 --> 00:22:02,896
正确读取平面图并从零开始构建一个动态场景，且不依赖任何库，这才是决定我是否真的愿意在周一早上交给它处理的任务。
Reading a floor plan correctly and building a moving scene from nothing with no libraries to lean on is the part that changes what I'd actually hand

256
00:22:03,056 --> 00:22:04,132
这就是关键点。
it on a Monday morning.

257
00:22:04,366 --> 00:22:06,576
让我烦心的是定价逻辑。
What annoys me is the pricing logic.

258
00:22:06,798 --> 00:22:12,452
你得为这个模型支付最高费率，而它的开发者却告诉你大部分时间都不该去用它。
You pay top rates for a model whose own maker tells you not to reach for it most of the time.

259
00:22:12,910 --> 00:22:18,496
至于你的任务到底落在那个界限的哪一边，完全要靠你自己判断。
And working out which side of that line your task falls on is left entirely to you.

260
00:22:18,766 --> 00:22:26,628
如果你想在一个窗口里同时对比 Claude、ChatGPT、Gemini 和 Grok 的提示词效果，这就是我开发 AI Master 的目的，
If you want to run a prompt against Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, and Grok side by side in one window, that's what I built AI Master

261
00:22:26,816 --> 00:22:28,228
链接就在下方。
for, and the link is below.

262
00:22:28,622 --> 00:22:30,016
我们下期见。
See you in the next one.

